===Etymology===
From {{proto|gem-pro|hwat|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|kʷos||kʷod|lang=ang}}. Cognates include Old Frisian [[hwet]], Old Saxon [[hwat]] (Dutch [[wat]]), Old High German [[hwaz]] (German [[was]]), Old Norse [[hvat]] (Swedish [[vad]]), Gothic [[𐍈𐌰]]. The Indo-European root also led to the Latin {{term|quod|lang=la}}, Lithuanian {{term|kad|kàd|lang=lt}}, and Irish {{term|cad|lang=ga}}.

